# Next Implementation Steps - Loyalty System

## Problem Analysis

Based on the current state assessment, the loyalty system has:

**Strengths:**
- ✅ Clean Architecture foundation with proper layering
- ✅ Rich domain entities with business logic  
- ✅ Value objects implemented (Address, GeoLocation, etc.)
- ✅ Strong-typed IDs using EntityId pattern
- ✅ Basic domain events infrastructure
- ✅ Repository and Unit of Work patterns
- ✅ Three API applications (Admin, Staff, Customer) with comprehensive controllers
- ✅ Build successful with 0 errors

**Current Gaps:**
- Missing Customer UI flows and backend endpoints (documented in `docs/Application Spec/Missing Customer UI Flows.md`)
- Incomplete DDD implementation (Phase 1 mostly complete, Phase 2 completed)
- Missing value objects: PersonalInfo, CommsPreferences, ConsentSet
- Need to enhance remaining entities (Reward, Transaction)
- Missing unit tests for new domain logic

## Solution Design

**Approach**: Continue with incremental DDD enhancement while implementing missing functionality

**Priority Order:**
1. Complete remaining DDD Phase 1 tasks (value objects, entity enhancements)
2. Implement critical missing Customer API endpoints
3. Add comprehensive unit tests
4. Begin Phase 3 of DDD migration (bounded context organization)

## Implementation Steps

### Phase 1: Complete DDD Domain Model Enhancement
- [ ] Create remaining value objects
  - [ ] PersonalInfo (customer data)
  - [ ] CommsPreferences (communication settings) 
  - [ ] ConsentSet (privacy consents)
- [ ] Enhance remaining entities
  - [ ] Reward entity with business rules
  - [ ] Transaction entity with validation
- [ ] Add comprehensive unit tests
  - [ ] Value object tests
  - [ ] Business rule tests
  - [ ] Domain event tests

### Phase 2: Implement Critical Missing Customer API Endpoints
- [ ] Transaction history endpoint (`GET /api/transactions`)
- [ ] Notification preferences (`PATCH /api/notifications/preferences`)
- [ ] Account accessibility settings (`PATCH /api/account/accessibility`)
- [ ] 2FA backup codes (`POST /api/account/2fa/backup-codes`, `GET /api/account/2fa/backup-codes`)
- [ ] Session management (`GET /api/account/sessions`, `POST /api/account/sessions/revoke-all`)

### Phase 3: Testing and Quality Assurance
- [ ] Unit tests for all new domain logic
- [ ] Integration tests for new API endpoints
- [ ] Performance testing of enhanced domain model
- [ ] Security testing of new endpoints

### Phase 4: Documentation Updates
- [ ] Update API documentation with new endpoints
- [ ] Document new domain model enhancements
- [ ] Update architecture documentation

## Affected Components

### Domain Layer
- `src/LoyaltySystem.Domain/ValueObjects/` - New value objects
- `src/LoyaltySystem.Domain/Entities/Reward.cs` - Business rule enhancements
- `src/LoyaltySystem.Domain/Entities/Transaction.cs` - Validation enhancements

### Application Layer
- `src/LoyaltySystem.Application/Services/` - Service enhancements for new endpoints
- `src/LoyaltySystem.Application/DTOs/` - New DTOs for missing endpoints

### API Layer
- `src/LoyaltySystem.Customer.API/Controllers/` - New endpoints implementation
- `src/LoyaltySystem.Admin.API/Controllers/` - Potential admin endpoints for new features

### Infrastructure Layer
- `src/LoyaltySystem.Infrastructure/Repositories/` - Repository enhancements if needed

### Testing
- `test/` - New unit and integration tests

## Dependencies

- No blocking dependencies identified
- Can proceed with Phase 1 immediately
- Phase 2 depends on Phase 1 completion for domain model stability

